//? Title: Monocular depth: explicit tensor metric-depth fitting
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
One RGB image must reveal metric scene depth despite ambiguous scale and missing sensor supervision. A global coarse field and local RGB refinement predict positive depth in meters. Hand log/neighbor checks precede genuine room-disjoint NYU raw sensor pairs,visible SGD priors and complete-model Adam,with immutable RGB-only restoration and every held-out room error shown.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.8_other_vision_tasks/monocular_depth.cpp`.

> The method

The observation is sampled RGB only. Positive coarse/refined heads emit meters;
log-depth losses use true sensor support and retain metric-scale supervision
at lambda.5. Valid-neighbor differences add local structure without treating
holes as edges. Separate fitting-only geometric/spatial log-depth parameters
provide explicit optimizer-based references. All numeric preprocessing,
objectives,inference,metrics and display values use tensors.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/monocular_depth_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/monocular_depth_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/monocular_depth_concept.tikz > build/monocular_depth_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/monocular_depth_concept.svg build/monocular_depth_concept.dvi > build/monocular_depth_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
