> Scale-invariant structure does not recover metric scale

Let e=log(prediction)-log(sensor). Per supported image,the source loss is
mean(e²)-lambda*mean(e)². Lambda0 gives log MSE;lambda1 removes a uniform
multiplicative scale error. Default lambda.5 retains scale supervision.
If prediction=alpha*truth everywhere,the loss is(1-lambda)*log(alpha)².
A two-times-depth prediction can therefore have zero scale-invariant error
while still having large metric RMSE and AbsRel. Evaluation applies no median
alignment or other target-derived scale correction.
```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/monocular_depth_scale.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  const auto scales = n::arange(.5, 2.001, .02, n::DType::Float64);
  const auto truth = n::ones({1, 2, 3, 1}, n::DType::Float64), mask = n::ones_like(truth);
  std::vector<double> mse, half, invariant;
  for (double scale : scales.to_vector<double>()) {
    mse.push_back(m::DepthLogLoss(truth * scale, truth, mask, 0.).item());
    half.push_back(m::DepthLogLoss(truth * scale, truth, mask, .5).item());
    invariant.push_back(m::DepthLogLoss(truth * scale, truth, mask, 1.).item());
  }
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.lines(scales.to_vector<double>(), mse, "lambda0", {37, 99, 235})
      .lines(scales.to_vector<double>(), half, "lambda.5", {220, 38, 38})
      .lines(scales.to_vector<double>(), invariant, "lambda1", {22, 163, 74})
      .title("Uniform scale error and log-depth loss")
      .x_label("prediction / true metric depth")
      .y_label("per-image masked log objective")
      .y_limits(-.03, .65)
      .size(950, 480);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  p.save_svg("build/monocular_depth_scale.svg");
  const auto score = m::ScoreTensorDepth(n::full({1, 1, 1, 1}, 2.), n::ones({1, 1, 1, 1}),
                                         n::ones({1, 1, 1, 1}));
  std::print("Twice true depth:AbsRel {},RMSE {}m,SILog {},delta1 {}. Scale invariance does "
             "not imply metric accuracy.\n",
             score.abs_rel.item(), score.rmse.item(), score.silog.item(), score.delta1.item());
}
```
