Twice true depth:AbsRel 1,RMSE 1m,SILog 0,delta1 0. Scale invariance does not imply metric accuracy.
\image(figures/monocular_depth_scale.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Uniform multiplicative scale error is retained at lambda0/.5 and removed at lambda1. Metric scores remain in meters without post-hoc GT alignment.)
\alttext(Uniform multiplicative scale error is retained at lambda0/.5 and removed at lambda1. Metric scores remain in meters without post-hoc GT alignment.)

> Sensor holes must not become artificial edges

The neighbor loss averages absolute log-residual differences only when both
endpoints have true sensor support. In the hand2x3 log-error field
[0,1,hole;0,1,2],five neighbor pairs are eligible,and their absolute differences
sum to3. The neighbor loss is therefore .6. Five valid samples have mean
error.8 and mean square1.2,so lambda.5 log loss is .88. The NaN hole is
selected out **before** logarithms,and its prediction derivative must be zero.
```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/monocular_depth_neighbors.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  const auto error = n::from_vector(std::vector<double>{0, 1, NAN, 0, 1, 2}, {1, 2, 3, 1});
  const auto truth = n::from_vector(std::vector<double>{1, 1, NAN, 1, 1, 1}, {1, 2, 3, 1});
  const auto prediction = n::exp(error).requires_grad_(), mask = n::ones_like(truth);
  const auto log = m::DepthLogLoss(prediction, truth, mask),
             neighbor = m::DepthGradientLoss(prediction, truth, mask);
  const auto gradient = n::grad(log + .1 * neighbor, {prediction})[0];
  const auto safe = m::DepthLogError(prediction, truth, mask);
  if (std::abs(log.item() - .88) > 1e-12 || std::abs(neighbor.item() - .6) > 1e-12 ||
      gradient.to_vector<double>()[2] != 0)
    return 1;
  auto a = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(safe.error.reshape({2, 3}), {0}), 0, 2),
       b = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(safe.valid.reshape({2, 3}), {0}), 0, 1);
  a.title("Safe log residual;hole stored as0")
      .x_label("column")
      .y_label("original row0 at bottom");
  b.title("True sensor support").x_label("column").y_label("original row0 at bottom");
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2);
  layout.add(a).add(b).size(1100, 500).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/monocular_depth_neighbors.svg");
  std::print("Five valid samples/pairs;log loss {:.2f},neighbor loss {:.2f},invalid "
             "prediction gradient {}.\n",
             log.item(), neighbor.item(), gradient.to_vector<double>()[2]);
}
```
