\caption(Twenty-four visible RGB-only Adam updates. The right panel shows weighted component contributions,which sum to the fitting total. Validation selects the checkpoint without test-derived scale correction.)
\alttext(Twenty-four visible RGB-only Adam updates. The right panel shows weighted component contributions,which sum to the fitting total. Validation selects the checkpoint without test-derived scale correction.)


\image(figures/monocular_depth_metrics.svg)
\caption(All16 held-out rooms compare learned refined/coarse metric depth with separately SGD-fitted geometric and spatial priors. Sensor masks,physical units and equal room weighting are identical for all estimates.)
\alttext(Held-out room RMSE and absolute-relative errors for RGB predictions and strong fitting-only depth references.)

\image(figures/monocular_depth_predictions.png)
\caption(All16 actual held-out rooms,two five-panel tiles per row. Each tile:observed RGB,true raw sensor colors,refined prediction colors,valid absolute error/5 red,and white sensor support. Black true-depth holes are unfilled. Numeric predictions remain raw even when their display colors saturate.)
\alttext(Original held-out NYU indoor RGB images,true sparse sensor depth,RGB-only predictions,errors and explicit validity masks.)

The refined RGB model has mean room RMSE1.388465m,compared with
1.304952m for the SGD geometric reference and1.117481m for the SGD spatial
reference. Its AbsRel is also worse than both priors. Thus this short fit
does not demonstrate an improvement in metric depth accuracy in new rooms. The true sensor holes,per-room weighting,physical error table and
strong fitting-only priors expose this limit. The model has no access to
sensor depth at inference and receives no target-derived scale correction.
This custom56-room baseline is not an original Eigen/pretrained model or
published NYU benchmark result.

> Conclusion

Positive-head,masked-log and valid-neighbor derivatives establish the local mechanism. Reproducible original RGB/raw sensor frames then support visible optimizer fits for both priors and every network leaf. RGB-only restored inference is immutable;room-level metrics,actual sensor holes and strong fitting-only references bound the short experiment’s claims.

> References

- [Eigen,Puhrsch and Fergus(2014),Depth Map Prediction from a Single Image using a Multi-Scale Deep Network](https://arxiv.org/abs/1406.2283).
- [Silberman et al.(2012),NYU Depth V2 dataset and aligned rawDepths documentation](https://cs.nyu.edu/~fergus/datasets/nyu_depth_v2.html).
- [Official NYU labeled Matlab/HDF5 archive](https://horatio.cs.nyu.edu/mit/silberman/nyu_depth_v2/nyu_depth_v2_labeled.mat).
